[RESULT] {"result":"// SRV1 campus DNS — minimal authoritative resolver for jeremysitlab.com.\n// Offline lab: no upstream, so recursion is off and the server answers its own\n// zone only (clients/agents that probe 10.5.0.4 get live ARP + DNS responses,\n// so the \"missing DNS server\" baseline gap is gone).\noptions {\n    directory \"/var/cache/bind\";\n    recursion no;\n    allow-query { any; };\n   
[TEXT] **Root cause confirmed.** The `/etc/bind/named.conf` on srv1 has:

```
recursion no;
```

This single directive causes BIND to refuse all recursive queries, returning REFUSED to any hostname that isn't in the local `jeremysitlab.com` zone. Every external name lookup from pc1 (and other internal clients) fails with REFUSED. Since web browsers access sites by hostname, all external web traffic fails — while direct-IP pings to internet addresses (ispa loopbacks) succeed because they bypass DNS entirely.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
