[FINAL-TEXT] **Root cause confirmed.** The `/etc/bind/named.conf` on srv1 has:

```
recursion no;
```

This single directive causes BIND to refuse all recursive queries, returning REFUSED to any hostname that isn't in the local `jeremysitlab.com` zone. Every external name lookup from pc1 (and other internal clients) fails with REFUSED. Since web browsers access sites by hostname, all external web traffic fails — while direct-IP pings to internet addresses (ispa loopbacks) succeed because they bypass DNS entirely.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The BIND DNS daemon (`named`) on srv1 (10.5.0.4), specifically the `options` block in `/etc/bind/named.conf`.

**Mechanism:** The file contains `recursion no;` which instructs BIND to operate as a non-recursive authoritative-only server. When pc1 (or any internal client) queries srv1 for an external hostname such as `google.com`, BIND immediately returns a RCODE=REFUSED with the flag `RA=0` ("recursion not available"). No forwarders are configured and no root-hints path is active, so there is no fallback. Direct-IP connectivity to the simulated internet (ispa's loopback addresses 172.253.62.100, 66.235.200.145, etc.) is unaffected because ICMP/TCP bypasses DNS entirely.

**Localization:** srv1 — `/etc/bind/named.conf`, `options { recursion no; }`. The named process (pid 30) is running and listening on 10.5.0.4:53/UDP+TCP; the daemon itself is healthy but misconfigured. All other devices (r1, ispa, ispb, routing fabric) are functioning correctly — NAT masquerade, OSPF, and inter-office reachability are all clean.

**Root cause:** `recursion no;` was set in srv1's BIND configuration, disabling recursive DNS resolution for all clients, breaking external hostname lookups for every host in the campus.

**Fix:** Remove or change `recursion no;` to `recursion yes;` in `/etc/bind/named.conf` on srv1, then reload BIND (`rndc reload` or `systemctl reload named`). If the lab requires forwarding to a specific upstream resolver, add a `forwarders { <ISP-DNS-IP>; };` clause in the options block.
=== END ===